e Campus Engagement & recognition Engagement & recognition Changemaker Awards Changemaker Awards Changemaker Award Nominations - Employees Peacock Awards Service awards Creating an engaging employee experience Human rights and accessibility Human rights and accessibility Accessibility Accessibility Our commitment to accessibility Resources for staff & faculty Staff profile: Donneil McNab Video & transcript President's Steering Committee on Equity, Diversity & Inclusion Reporting on diversity Get involved Indigenous engagement Volunteering & giving Volunteering & giving Donating blood United Way at Royal Roads United Way at Royal Roads United Way prize options Meet the United Way committee United Way events Your impact Your impact Donation matching with United Way Seeking a new United Way campaign chair United Way news Our university Top Header Menu Programs & courses Admission Current students Resource catalogue Crossroads Departments Careers Forms RoyalRoads.ca Log in Search Breadcrumb Home Departments People and Culture Departments People and Culture Contact People and Culture Employee & labour relations People and Culture commitment & expectations People and Culture team IT Services Faculty Affairs Our vision statement People and Culture provide leadership in shaping an equitable and inclusive culture that drives diversity, excellence, and innovation by supporting talent, engagement, and the employee work experience as we work together to achieve the university's goals. Learn more about People and Culture at RRU Our commitment & expectations People and Culture aims to create the best possible workplace for employee groups at RRU. We support each other as we strive to achieve the university's goals. Our team Meet the People and Culture team at Royal Roads University. We're here to help current and prospective staff and faculty. Send us an email. Contact People and Culture Royal Roads University's People and Culture Office is open weekdays from 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Contact us by sending us an email, and we'll respond shortly. Employee & labour relations RRU commits to good relations with staff and faculty both in and outside of bargaining units. We keep the university community up to date on labour matters. People and Culture policies View RRU's HR and employment policies, including those governing leaves of absence, compensation, stipends, tuition assistance and vacation. Contact People and Culture Send us an email @ Royal Roads Location 2005 Sooke Road Victoria, BC  V9B 5Y2 Canada Campus map Contact Phone: 250.391.2511 Toll-free: 1.800.788.8028 Contact directory Popular links Careers Campus Security IT Services Multimedia Services Webmail Policies Follow us Facebook Instagram Linkedin Youtube © 2026 Royal Roads University | Footer Website feedback"
